synopsis:
  `runGhc/runGhcT` no longer hijack process signals, old behaviour provided by
  `runGhcWithSignalHandlers`.
description:
  Functions `runGhc/runGhcT` no longer go out of their way to redirect process
  signals as exceptions to them.

  The installed handlers make it so other threads are unaware of any signals,
  which can cause the process to become unresponsive whenever a crash of the GHC
  session(s) does not cascade into a shutdown of the process itself.

  The old behaviour is available through `runGhcWithSignalHandlers` or by
  calling `withSignalHandlers`. Only intended to be used from the main thread of
  your process, see the documentation.
